{
  "summary": "Exposes the internal `PubkeyProvider` struct in `descriptor.h` and adds a public `ParsePubkey` function for parsing standalone key expressions using P2TR rules. Adds a `GetOriginInfo()` accessor to inspect derivation path and fingerprint information on parsed providers. Also fixes `musig()` descriptor parsing to reject unexpected trailing characters.",
  "problem": "Callers such as wallet setup wizards cannot validate or inspect standalone descriptor key expressions without wrapping them into full descriptors, as key expression parsing and `PubkeyProvider` are internal to `descriptor.cpp`. Additionally, `musig()` parser logic erroneously ignored unexpected characters after the closing parenthesis if they did not follow valid derivation syntax.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'This is particularly useful in GUI multisig setup flows where the UI accepts a pasted key expression. The GUI can use this parser to validate input, inspect the parsed key, and apply setup-specific policy i.e. reject private keys, uncompressed keys etc. (Multisig Wizard tracking issue: #35645)'",
    "Commit 33af6fdbc1: 'The musig() parser split the input at the closing parenthesis without validating the remaining text. This allowed unexpected characters after the expression to be ignored.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": [
      "#35645"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Moving `PubkeyProvider` from `descriptor.cpp` to `descriptor.h` is primarily a move-only refactor of internal types into a header.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Exposes the PubkeyProvider interface and introduces a public ParsePubkey function to parse and inspect individual descriptor key expressions under P2TR rules. This allows components such as the GUI multisig setup wizard (#35645) to validate pasted key expressions and extract key origin info without constructing dummy descriptors. It also fixes a descriptor parsing bug where trailing characters after musig() expressions were ignored rather than rejected.",
